# Hide game and rotation controls while editing

Remove the burger menu and both Board rotation actions from edit mode while retaining them in view mode.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] View mode continues to show burger menu, rotate-left, and rotate-right side by side at the upper-left in that order.
- [x] Entering edit mode removes the burger-menu button from the visible and accessible hierarchy.
- [x] Entering edit mode removes both rotation buttons from the visible and accessible hierarchy.
- [x] No empty control row or reserved spacing remains beneath the Terrain/Numbers selector after removal.
- [x] Terrain/Numbers, Help, player selection, and Done retain their existing edit-mode behavior.
- [x] Leaving edit mode restores all three view-mode controls immediately.
- [x] Hiding the controls does not change the persisted Board orientation.
- [x] New Game remains available through the burger menu in view mode.
- [x] SCR-001 is updated to remove its superseded edit-mode rotation instruction before implementation is completed.
- [x] UI regression coverage compiles.
- [ ] Focused mode-transition checks pass on a functioning simulator or device.

## Scope notes

- This task supersedes the TASK-038 criterion that kept rotation controls beneath the edit selector.
- Rotation behavior in view mode is refined separately by TASK-044.

## Evidence

- Conditioned the complete menu/rotation control row on view mode and removed the former edit-mode rotation row.
- Updated SCR-001 and UI coverage for disappearance on Edit and immediate restoration on Done.
- Preserved orientation state and all remaining edit controls.
- Arm64 simulator-target `xcodebuild build-for-testing` succeeded.
